• Done. Final report: files changed, instrument numbers, baseline table.

• Done. Committed as `ec42686` on `gauntlet/bench2` (not pushed).

  ## Files changed

  - `bench/run.sh` — new `--stream <domain>` flag: swaps `bench/issues/` for `bench/streams/<domain>/`, runs tasks in `meta.json` `order`, works with `--tasks`/`--verify-fixtures`/`--leak-check`/`--out`. Also a robustness fix: results dirs now carry the PID (`<ts>-<pid>`), because two parallel stream runs starting in the same second used to share `records.tsv` and corrupt each other's summary. JSON output gains a `"stream"` field.
  - `bench/agents/slag-fix.sh` — now runs the real `slag fix --no-commit` via `SLAG_BIN`; `SLAG_FIX_TRIES` (default 1) keeps the baseline on the base model, not retries on the plan model.
  - `bench/streams/py-data/01..08` and `bench/streams/js-web/01..08` — 16 tasks, same layout as `bench/issues/`, plus `order` and `traps` in `meta.json`. Recurring traps per domain: py-data leans on exact-input reproduction, tz-naive datetimes, unicode normalization, Decimal ROUND_HALF_UP, CSV edge cases; js-web on URL/query semantics, async ordering, 1-based pagination, cache key normalization/stale writes, swallowed errors. 2 easy / 4 medium / 2 hard each, ordered easy to hard.
  - `bench/results/stream-baseline-py-data.json`, `bench/results/stream-baseline-js-web.json`
  - `bench/README.md` — stream mode, executor choice, baseline table.

  ## Instrument checks

  - `--verify-fixtures`: all 16 stream tasks pass (hidden fails on buggy repo, passes after `reference.patch`); the classic 8 still pass.
  - Leak probe: clean on both streams and the default set (issue alone in temp dir, no bench paths in env).
  - noop: 0/8 per stream, 0/8 classic (0/16 on streams). reference: 8/8 per stream, 8/8 classic (16/16 on streams).

  ## Baseline (slag v2.9.0, `slag fix --tries 1`)

  | model | py-data | js-web | verdict |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | mistral/ministral-8b-latest | (mostly pass) | 7/8 | too strong, no headroom |
  | openai/gpt-4.1-nano | 5/8 | 4/8 | uneven, slightly strong |
  | **mistral/ministral-3b-latest** | **2/8** | **2/8** | chosen, 25% on each |

  Chosen executor baseline, ministral-3b-latest:

  - py-data PASS: `01-csv-bom` (26s), `03-tz-filter` (25s); FAIL on money-round, unicode-dedupe, csv-quoted-newline, float-total, dst-schedule, csv-chunk-boundary.
  - js-web PASS: `03-pager-offbyone` (37s), `05-url-join` (17s); FAIL on query-decode, cache-params-order, async-order, fetch-error-swallow, cache-stale-race, cursor-pagination.

  Failure modes are the kind a harness can learn from: the model often passes slag's own verification but misses the held-out behavior (e.g. partial query decoding), or writes analysis with no edit. Total spend stayed well under $2 (cheap presets, ~40k tokens per task).

  One deviation to note: I ran candidate baselines in parallel after fixing the runner collision; earlier polluted output was discarded and regenerated cleanly.

